{"name":"Safflower Red","hex":"#d9333f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"safflower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cultivated thistle-like plant, Carthamus tinctorius, family Asteraceae, now grown mainly for its oil."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safflower"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carthamin","blocks":[{"text":"Carthamin is a natural red pigment derived from safflower, earlier known as carthamine. It is used as a dye and a food coloring. As a food additive, it is known as Natural Red 26."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Carthamin.png/330px-Carthamin.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carthamin","wikidata":"Q419193"},{"title":"Safflower","blocks":[{"text":"Safflower, also false saffron, is a highly branched, herbaceous, thistle-like annual plant in the family Asteraceae. It is one of the world's oldest crops; today, it is commercially cultivated for vegetable oil extracted from the seeds. Plants are 30 to 150 cm tall with globular flower heads having yellow, orange, or red flowers. Each branch will usually have from one to five flower heads containing 15 to 20 seeds per head. Safflower is native to arid environments having seasonal rain. It grows a deep taproot which enables it to thrive in such environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Safflower.jpg/330px-Safflower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safflower","wikidata":"Q156625"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Carthamin_proposed_biosynthesis.png/500px-Carthamin_proposed_biosynthesis.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Carthamin_proposed_biosynthesis.png/500px-Carthamin_proposed_biosynthesis.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarthamin_proposed_biosynthesis.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Illustration_Carthamus_tinctorius0.jpg/500px-Illustration_Carthamus_tinctorius0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Illustration_Carthamus_tinctorius0.jpg/1280px-Illustration_Carthamus_tinctorius0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe